00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:01.309 align:start position:0%
 
the doom games have always been  jam-packed with Easter eggs and eternal  may have them most of all so with that  in mind I try to dig out as many Easter  eggs and secrets as I could find the  best place to start is in the doom  Slayers Workshop / office / library  where there is a plethora of toy details  that could potentially be easily missed  one of the first things that may catch  your eye is the adorable portrait of the  doom Slayer and his beloved rabbit Daisy  she appeared in the original doom having  met an unfortunate end as the demons  arrived from hell while the painting is  a touching homage we live in hope that  days will return to the doom fortress as  the Slayer also has a bag of food and a  hutch ready for her arrival rumor is  that Daisy will also appear in every  level of doom eternal although so far I  found her in just the one outside the  throne room of King Novik have you found  her anywhere else well then make sure to  leave it in the comments now Daisy's  reappearance was also teased by the doom  Twitter account in a post reading  justice for Daisy and again as the  adorable little rabbit was hiding in  this cover image there has always been a  theme of referencing older age software  games with Commander Keen popping up  more than once his helmet and I guess  skull adorns the top of the bookshelf  along with his blaster his portrait also  appears as the mascot for some of the  snacks you can find littered around the  ruined earth alongside one of the  enemies of the Commander Keen series the  dopefish this strange buck-toothed fish  first appeared in 1991 s Commander Keen  secret of the Oracle but an eternal also  features as a snack food mascot as well  as apparently being a chainsaw  manufacturer if you inspect the chainsaw  from your weapon wall you can see more  of the dopefish details or you can get  much closer in the first part of the  contest base level and blow the poor guy  up for an extra life back to the Slayers  chaotic desk though next to a copy of  demonology today is an empty pizza box  featuring the handsome visage of its  creative director  Hugo Martin this box also appeared in  doom 2016 but now it seems he's  diversified his food range with his own  brand of jerky - keeping on the topic of  foodstuffs a packet of lanes takoyaki  flavor chips is also on the desk while  the name and logo is a reference to the  real world brand Lay's it's also a  reference to dooms lead concept artist  John Lane a piece of concept art there  was seemingly Dunford  sixteen has found life as doom Slayers  mouse mats and his name features wants  more on the rest of the chip bags found  back on earth  strange flavors though as you can see  the Slayers computer monitor has some  interesting file names and folders on  his desktop personally I'm most into  seeing the shotgun portraits folder and  instead of your average office toy he  has the soul cube from doom 3 just to  hanging out on his desk in Doom 3 it was  an extremely powerful weapon killing  most enemies in one hits and  replenishing the players health so  either it's an ER or it's a replica and  if not we are really hoping maybe we'll  get to use the spinning box of death  once more in dooms future one of the  comics that stood out to me in this room  was one titled hell Walker a title that  the dream Slayer is sometimes known as  it features a design and font extremely  similar to that of the Hellboy graphic  novels but instead featuring one of  eternal Marauders on the cover this  comic as well as others found in the  room are published by the Tackett comics  group Flynn fly Taggart was actually the  protagonist in the 1990s doom novels  knee-deep in the dead hell on earth  infernal sky and endgame the peculiar  cookbook underneath it featuring an  original team Cacodemons sprite is  titled Kadeem gear cooking Gdynia is an  ancient Sumerian word for Babylon and  used in doom 2016 for the first level in  which players visited Hell in Kittinger  sanctum Gdynia sanctum is also referred  to as the Blood Keith perhaps suggesting  that this is a word for one of the  locations that these demons reside and  as such is simply a recipe book for some  good old-fashioned demon's home cooking  flavors to remind them of home I guess  of course you also have the iconic doom  2016 soundtrack on vinyl a version of  both on tape and an old-school 1960s PC  that you can actually play the original  doom on that is if you find all the  secret cheat discs in the campaign  speaking of vinyls if you find any of  the world be sure to check the framed  images back base they're all tracks from  its game library including classic  bangers from Wolfenstein 3d and  Commander Keen finally tucked away on  the right is a skateboard a little odd  for a slayer to have sure but I think it  may be a reference to the bizarre time  we're doomed guy was an unlockable  character in the PC version of Tony  Hawk's Pro Skater 3 now as to the  Slayers more musical hobbies doom has  always had ties to heavy metal and  playing on that there are three guitars  hung on the wall in three distinct  styles but take the count of each string  and you  six-six-six that's pretty metal for  anyone wondering about the redesign of  the plasma rifle between 2016 and  eternal the spare parts on his desk may  suggest that the pistol and plasma rifle  from the previous game and now in bits  and pieces but fun fact view the new  plasma rifle is based on the design of  the original team's weapon which itself  was made from a digitized image of the  Rambo m60 toy gun we really have come  full circle moving to this lays  impressive book collection each spine of  every book holds a reference to either a  game classical literature or the wider  gaming community here are a few choice  nods to some classic novels eat ripped  hair instead of Eat Pray Love the man in  the high argent tower instead of man in  the high castle and the kakko in the Rye  instead of The Catcher in the Rye the  middle shelf however has a lot more  modern references my buddy Superfly is a  reference to daikatana written by the  game's protagonist to honor the AI  companion to Superfly Johnson why I'm so  great by dork Norcom is of course a  reference to duke nukem devilish daggers  and other assorted pointy objects is a  nod to the game devil daggers a game  that takes a lot of inspiration from the  FPS games of the 90s and drops you into  an arena fighting hordes of demons  leAndria a brief history of  interplanetary industry is a reference  to the Leandre cooperation from the  Unreal Tournament series the Von Braun  book takes its name from one of the  interplanetary ships from System Shock  to Mesa science monthly predicting  unforeseen consequences takes its name  from half-life's Black Mesa site and the  title of the third chapter unforeseen  consequences the unit code training  manual for bomb defusal is a reference  to the original deus ex and the in-game  faction the United Nations  anti-terrorist coalition the spear of  destiny a post-war deconstruction refers  to the edge software Wolfenstein 3d  prequel the spear of destiny living with  rage is of course a connection to one of  its other FPS franchises the rage series  the strog are one of the races from the  quake series this book perhaps being a  reference to the brutal struggle ocation  process from quake 4 retcon the life and  times of flint agate seems to confirm  that the novel protagonist i mentioned  earlier is indeed no longer canon sorry  about that fly the dopefish returns  again in from nope fish to dope fish  tight hangar a guides off world travel  is a reference to a planet that appeared  in the original doom bible design  document in  preliminary parts of creation doomed the  game was going to take place on this  fictional planet rather than the moons  of Mars the next book shares a title  with the fourth and final level of  ultimate doom thy flesh consumed to pray  or not to pray is from well the pray  series interestingly though the 2006  game used it Tech for the same engine as  doom 3 and the 2017 game featured music  from the same composer as doom Mick  Gordon the vault dweller Survival Guide  is a direct reference to the Fallout  series and being safely guided by the  doom Slayer figure from the 2016 game is  a touching a Marge - markiplier as  father Clifton Morris Fischbach mark has  been a longtime doom fan and the title  of the book being how to comb your  moustache is fitting as from what I've  seen that man really did have a great -  and of course the rest of the space on  the Shelf is taken up by some classic  entries in the FPS genre dream also has  some pretty weird symbols complete with  its own demonic language but one stood  out to me as I was skewering this man  cubis on the tip of the Slayers spear  that appears to be a version of the  chemical symbol for sulfur associated  with a fire and brimstone of hell now  this may not be an easter egg but will  likely be something that not many  players will notice but if you go into  your game settings there is an option  for not only the classic gun poses but  also the classic sound effects this will  position your weapons in the middle of  the screen and let you pretend you're  playing a way shinier version of the  doom games of old  now these two eggs and references beyond  this point may have some spoilers to the  story of doom eternal so consider  yourself warned  so if you've been playing doom eternal  then you've no doubt noticed this toy  hanging out in the middle of your  fortress of doom if you be every Slayer  gate and collect every key you'll be  able to unlock the super weapon known as  the young maker this is one of the  things that ties doom eternal to doom 64  were a weapon of a similar name and  function but a much fleshy er design is  usable so it appears that a slayer may  have kept it for a rainy day  again potential spoilers but my theory  is that one of the doom mothers you  fight in doom 64 and at the climax of  the new level release alongside eternal  go on to become the card maker herself  especially since her visage is somewhat  more demonic after the completion of her  boss fight and I think my favorite  Easter Egg dye found so far takes place  during this cutscene where the doom  Slayer has his flashback as he's been  dragged to the priests and mumbling in  his own rage he says guts huge guts  which is a reference to the 16-page 1996  doom comic where our protagonist comes  face to face with a cyberdemon and  screams you are huge that means you have  huge guts rip and tear I definitely  didn't expect to be thinking about that  let's say interesting comic when I sat  through that cutscene and if you stay  tuned to the end of this video you can  find the very silly doom eternal  post-credits sequence something I missed  during my first playthrough so be sure  to stick around for that alright so  those are all the Easter eggs references  and cool things I've found so far have I  missed any almost absolutely doom has  always been full to the brim with Easter  eggs so I'm sure more will be found soon  if you have any yourself leave them in  the comment section below and we may do  a follow-up video of all the ones we  have yet to find but if you still have a  doom eternal itch we have plenty of  content for you including a nightmare  mode guide intense hoodless gameplay and  tips and tricks to keep you slaying so  for all that and more make sure you head  to GameSpot

